{{also|Deter}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|dēterreō||deter, discourage}}, from {{m|la|de||from}} + {{m|la|terreō||I frighten}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/dɪˈtɜː(ɹ)/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-deter.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɜː(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|++}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[prevent]] something from happening.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[persuade]] someone not to do something; to [[discourage]].
#: {{ux|en|Their boss '''deterred''' them from both taking holidays at the same time, claiming he couldn't manage it all on his own.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2020 July 1|author=Paul Stephen|title=Vital Connections|journal=Rail|page=41|text=Such a male-dominated environment is also likely to contribute to the lingering presence of an outdated belief that expressing feelings and demonstrating emotion is a sign of weakness, '''deterring''' some men from discussing their problems.}}
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=September 9, 2022
|author=Sameer Yasir
|title=2 Years After Deadly Fistfights, India and China Pull Back From Border
|journal=w:The New York Times
|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220909112326/https://www.nytimes.com/2022/09/09/world/asia/india-china-border.html
|archivedate=09 September 2022
|issn=0362-4331
|oclc=1645522
|section=Asia Pacific
|url2=https://archive.is/WBIkK
|text=Among the remaining contention points between the two armies is an eastern region called the Depsang Plains. Military analysts said that the Chinese Army was not allowing Indian troops to patrol in that area, even though they have done so for decades. While India’s military is already stretched thin, said Saurav Jha, editor in chief of the Delhi Defense Review, it still needs to keep up a permanent patrol to '''deter''' China.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[distract]] someone from something.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1748|author=David Hume|title=Enquiries concerning the human understanding and concerning the principles of moral.|location=London|publisher=Oxford University Press|year_published=1973|section=§ 10
|passage=we have in following enquiry, attempted to throw some light upon subjects, from which uncertainty has hitherto '''deterred''' the wise}}

